---
/**
 * The consent declaration, and the only analytics code in a layout.
 *
 * ── Why this exists at all ──
 * The site used to measure only the traffic that clicked Accept.
 * `injectTrackers()` was a switch: all three trackers or none. Everyone
 * who declined, and everyone who ignored the notice, was not
 * under-counted but absent.
 *
 * The switch is gone. Measurement now runs for every visitor, and the
 * notice informs rather than gates -- see CookieConsent.astro, whose
 * copy was rewritten to say so plainly.
 *
 * ── Why a consent declaration at all, if it is always granted ──
 * Because gtag.js asks. With no `consent default` on the page, Google
 * Ads and GA4 fall back to an undeclared state (`gcs=G1--`), which
 * degrades conversion modelling on the linked Ads account. Declaring
 * granted is a statement, not a gate: it costs one call, it is the
 * honest description of what this site does, and it is the single line
 * to edit if a jurisdiction ever has to be carved out. The `region`
 * parameter is how that carve-out would be written.
 *
 * ── Why it is `is:inline` and in the head ──
 * Astro defers processed <script> tags. A consent default that arrives
 * after the tag it governs is not a consent default. This must execute
 * during head parse, before gtag.js runs, which `is:inline` guarantees
 * and a processed script does not.
 *
 * ── What does NOT live here ──
 * HubSpot and Clarity. They load from CookieConsent.astro, which owns
 * tracker injection. This file declares consent and loads exactly one
 * Google tag. Nothing may add a second.
 */
const GA4_ID = 'G-5WYSWY2G6Z';
---
<script is:inline define:vars={{ GA4_ID }}>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag() { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); }
  window.gtag = gtag;

  // Granted, for everyone, immediately. There is deliberately no
  // `wait_for_update` here: that parameter exists to hold the tag while
  // an answer is fetched, and we are not waiting for one. Verified in a
  // browser against the live property -- a default carrying
  // `wait_for_update` with no update ever arriving suppresses the
  // collect request outright, so the parameter is not free.
  gtag('consent', 'default', {
    ad_storage: 'granted',
    ad_user_data: 'granted',
    ad_personalization: 'granted',
    analytics_storage: 'granted',
  });

  gtag('js', new Date());
  gtag('config', GA4_ID);
</script>
<script is:inline async src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${GA4_ID}`}></script>
